  "title": "Battle of Shanhai Pass, 1644",
  "summary": "At Shanhai Pass in late May 1644, the Ming general Wu Sangui and the Manchu regent Dorgon defeated the rebel army of Li Zicheng, who had taken Beijing in April. Dorgon entered Beijing on 6 June, opening the way to Qing rule over China proper.",
